I have a question that applies generically to different flavors of
unix.  Particularly, I am interested in possible SVR4 and OSF/1
implementation of the following:

In AIX, it is very easy to extend the set of kernel services that are
available to a user process.  These kernel services can "export" a set
of system calls that are available to user processes, thus extending
the function of the kernel in a manner that I as the programmer see
fit.

So the question is, is there some way in SVR4 or OSF/1 to do this
type of kernel extension.  That is, can I somehow provide a set of
functions (system calls) that are located in kernel space, that have
their interfaces available to a user application.  (This concept is
similar to the open/read/write/close/ioctl interface that is provided
to device driver writers today.)

