Concurrent use licenses are now available for Digital's major compiler
products on OpenVMS VAX, OpenVMS AXP and DEC OSF/1 AXP.  Each concurrent use
license allows the compiler to be used by one user at a time; additional users
can be added by adding more licenses.  Unlike personal use licenses,
concurrent use licenses are not restricted to a particular named user.  This
new licensing option can make Digital's compilers more affordable for many
customers, as compared to traditional capacity licensing.

Concurrent use licensing lets you use a product anywhere on a cluster or on 
a standalone system, regardless of the size of the processor. A concurrent 
use license is valid on both VAX and Alpha AXP systems under the same 
operating system -- so you can use, for example, a Fortran license on either 
an OpenVMS VAX or an OpenVMS AXP system.

The following product versions or later contain the appropriate License 
Management Facility calls to allow concurrent use:

                 OpenVMS VAX    OpenVMS AXP    DEC OSF/1 AXP

DEC Ada          V3.0A          V3.0A          V3.1
DEC C            V4.0           V1.3A          *
