|>Hi everybody,
|>
|>I'm trying to compile a X/Motif application on an alpha station
|>running OSF1 V1.3.
|>At link time, I got this ld error (running gcc V2.5.5):
|>
|>/bin/ld:
|>Error: Undefined:
|>dnet_conn
|>dnet_addr
|>getnodebyname
|>_DYNAMIC
|>collect2: ld returned 1 exit status

Add the following to the list of libraries on the compile:

	-ldnet_stub

The Motif and X11 contain support for DECNET as a transport.  Since there
is no way of knowing in advance whether or not a given DEC OSF/1 system
actually has DECNET or not, the dnet_stub library resolves all the DECNET
routines.  On systems that contain DECNET the stubs arrange to automatically
call the real DECNET routines if the application tries to use DECNET as
a transport.

-- 

				Frank


