Ian Leonard (leonardi@dpud.DIALiz.oz.au) wrote:
: Is there any software available for reading VMS backup savesets on either
: OSF/1 or ULTRIX ?  I have a copy of a utility called vmsbackup, but the
: format of the header in a saveset seems to have changed since this was
: written and it keeps failing with invalid header blocksize.  Is there
: an updated version of this available ?

The problem is a very simple one! In vmsbackup lots of things are declared as
long, which is a 32-bit quantity on most platforms, but on the Alpha longs
are 64 bits! The fix it to edit the vmsbackup.c source and replace long with 
int and rebuild. 

If you have any problems I think that there should be a copy of the version
I ported to Alpha and Solaris on sux1.sr.bham.ac.uk in pub/vmsbackup, you will
have to build it as the executable in the tar file is the Solaris one. N.B.
this is an extended vmsbackup which does a better job of big files and
has a more friendly pattern matching (case insensitive and better dealing
with directories).

