In article <2ol1a1$67i@ccu2.auckland.ac.nz> bruce-b@cs.aukuni.ac.nz (Bruce Benson) writes:
>/usr/ucb/mail on our alpha is the same as /bin/mail. Does anyone
>have ucbmail available or know where I can get the source?

On most systems, /bin/mail and /usr/bin/mail are the old version 7
mail program, now just used for local delivery of mail, and 
/usr/ucb/[Mm]ail is the mail reading program. On these systems as
long as you put /usr/ucb on your PATH before /usr/bin, you can just type
'mail' and get what you want.

Under OSF/1, /usr/ucb is a symlink to /usr/bin, so /usr/ucb/mail and
/usr/bin/mail are the same thing, and /usr/bin/Mail is the mail reader. 
So you now have to distinguish between 'mail' and 'Mail', regardless 
of your path (definitely not what most people are used to). I think if 
you invoke 'Mail', you'll get what you want.
-harry
