  Thanks To Bill G. from Dec, the solution is easy. I overlooked some
linker flags. My (well, my user's) fortran code calls exp() with
large negative numbers. I used by a misstake the single precision
library on the OpenVMS machine, which returns 0 for x<-85, on the
OSF machine the double precision library call returns zero for x<-700. 
Many of my numbers fell between these two limits so the OSF machine
did calculate a lot, the OpenVMS machine just returned zero.
  Just for the record. I got my expected speed compiling as:
f77 -o mycode mycode.for -non_shared -math_library fast
