|>Token ring is also a 48 bit address.  For some arcane reason it gets
|>transmitted using an opposite bit order than does Ethernet and FDDI,
|>but your example code won't see that difference.

Actually, TR and FDDI both transmit destination/source addresses in non-canonical
(MSB) format on the wire.  However, since most (all?) FDDI chipsets offer bit-
swapping in HW, most FDDI drivers present and expect addresses in canonical
(LSB) format, like Ethernet.
