There are a number of issues with X11R5 that makes it very
difficult to port to Alpha AXP.  Here're a couple:

	* X11R5 isn't 64-bit safe
		There are a number of places in R5 that assume
		that sizeof(int) == sizeof(long).  There must be
		thousands of places where this is the case. 
		Digital has provided the X Consortium with all
		of the code diffs required to make this work, and
		it will appear in X11R6, which will be available
		to non-Consortium members at the end of April, 1994.

	* X11R5 doesn't have any Alpha-capable DDX's
		Well, this isn't exactly true.  You may be able to
		make the SFB act as a dumb frame buffer, but since
		Alpha doesn't have a byte write, each write to the
		frame buffer would have to be a read-modify-write.

So, the long and the short, is: wait until R6 comes out, and use R6
instead.

