Comparing Digital's MP quality in the upcoming OSF MP release to any
experiences with other MP unix machines is totally unfair, particularly
some of the major unix variants.
 
Solaris, based on Sys V Rel 4.0.  USL quickly dumped 4.0 in favor of
4.1 and 4.2 particularly to gain SMP capability.  4.0 was NOT designed
to do SMP, but it was way too late for SUN to change to the newer
USL code base.
 
HP-UX, never designed to do SMP
 
AIX, never designed to do SMP
 
As I understand it, the UNI in UNIX is for UNI-Processor, a take off
from the name of the old MULTICS project, which was multi processing.
 
Digital has a horrible reputation in the UNIX market, partly well-deserved,
mostly unfair (IMO).
 
They absolutely CANNOT AFFORD to expose their unix customer's to
anything resembling other early smp unix efforts.
 
We are using OSF as a base, which was always intended to do SMP,
we have had it in house for YEARS, and we currently have all of our
best SMP experts working the code.
 
I challenge anyone to buy the early ship SMP units in April-June
and prove me wrong.
 
Digital's success depends on our SMP unix success (IMO), so I hope
customer's will be pleasantly surprised at having a new MP alternative
with serious performance in the very near future.
