>guys, and/or things to watch out for before I do the installation?

The DSP3210 probably looks a whole lot like the RZ28.  Still, disklabel
appears to be smart enough to not care.  I believe that if you use
an unrecognized name, disklabel will look up the partition table
information and geometry itself:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c dsp3210

It doesn't have anyway to get the correct speed, so you may want
to edit the label to put the right value (5400 I think).  Once
the label has the partition and geometry information filled in
newfs(8) doesn't even a disk type argument.

# newfs /dev/rrz#c

